  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_9e11bb72977644249752f46b28cf3b3e",
      "statement": "celld validates three promises — an acknowledged write is durable, a cell has one writer at a time, and Cloudflare Workers/Durable Objects code operates the same on celld — by breaking each at the layer where the failure shows most clearly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L3-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3c4a1ecc98a4e3b13bb5b488fdb636de9b3cefdc98834259b5ddf7d5a78d462b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c5df248f4fc64cde9c7251b3b5a7ff70",
      "statement": "The compatibility promise is tested differentially: each program runs once on workerd and once on celld on identical bytes and the outputs must be equal, so a test cannot agree with celld's own runtime by accident.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L17-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:678091183117ff8515f5ec015a3b2e907d55ec7624020ec1c47f63ddb6fed517:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_95e8643056434b63990d044c08f21231",
      "statement": "The conformance corpus only grows: new API surfaces add fixtures that must give equal output on workerd and celld, and the suites build into the binary under celld_internal_tests via include! in crates/celld/lib.rs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/lib.rs#L365-L430",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bd3916287ba0c544930c2b0605223dbf739ee7c51b09e2ea2834e98786640462:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L27-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f3ec8371b63e27f4b551340c5ac549a4710d58c1199cd8697cb24e4112bd156b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_956d3005d3f941a48a5572a68dabbd65",
      "statement": "The coordination protocol is specified in TLA+ and exhaustively model-checked at a small configuration, visiting every reachable state with a linearizable store and perfect clocks; the invariants are one writer per epoch and no acknowledged write lost.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L35-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:717fc93e10064a554198630ef3103be5fb6926df45a84c1f6b90d1c89b477514:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_445a1a7b5573481293419d467dbded79",
      "statement": "Every TLA+ configuration carries a pinned expected verdict and most are failures modeling past bugs, so a configuration that stops failing has lost its tooth.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L55-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f41478c8530cec1b04215fc601ed02986513fc7c0a6284abd91775efaf0f6cf3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_50e0e0a14b974f99ace205b0840f7c38",
      "statement": "The coordination protocol is a pure decision core with no I/O of its own, so a deterministic simulator injects latency, CAS races, and lost responses and crashes a node at each await point.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L88-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4891ee0459d034af26f1745d0b6efa6be1abec109dfffe38798783b0aa9ea46b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ccee6395ee3f4ca4b16be8f07b42b2f4",
      "statement": "A seeded scheduler drives each simulation run so a failure replays exactly with its seed; the properties cover safety and liveness and must survive tens of thousands of seeds (the core protocols have run millions).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L96-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:08d29c88cf4a167262f670aaef280e55f9a895df0caf1c1a73523caab88eb857:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f212ecef07a64c3ca2ad215e4b82dd8f",
      "statement": "The checkers are tested by running deliberately broken variants against the properties, so a suite that stays green against a broken protocol is a broken suite.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L105-L109",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:396098ef32250ed48e32bf9b34c74cac4828571c93092355189cba7168a42e27:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9efc4b54fbac4236ab9c7f8fb8ea010d",
      "statement": "A live fleet lab runs standard VMs with a real bucket and injects faults between verification passes, covering SIGKILL mid-write, freeze/unfreeze, bucket cutoff, 429 throttling, and host kill, across which no acknowledged write was lost and no committed state was damaged.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L111-L155",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ff2fe85af47e5d57c3ea391ab9b8bcda9dbbbf27eebef5e3ce819db3bd95222b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5ef4560d51ac49c6aa7c26d6033aa097",
      "statement": "Each published number carries its measurement conditions; notable results include 500 claimants with one writer per epoch over 5,500 attempts, a warm resident request doing zero bucket operations at ~1.1ms p50/~7ms p99, and ten small nodes holding 10,000 resident cells and 20,000 WebSockets.",
      "evidence": [
